---
import TutorialLayout from '../../../layouts/TutorialLayout.astro';
---

<TutorialLayout
  title="MPC: Fixed-Wing Aircraft"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { label: 'Tutorials', href: '/tutorials' },
    { label: 'Optimization & MPC', href: '/tutorials' },
    { label: 'MPC: Fixed-Wing' },
  ]}
  prev={{ label: 'MPC: Quadrotor', href: '/tutorials/optimization/mpc-quadrotor' }}
>
  <div class="p-6 rounded-xl bg-surface border border-border mb-8">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-text mb-2">Coming Soon</h2>
    <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
      This tutorial will walk through model predictive control for a fixed-wing aircraft (SportCub) &mdash;
      from writing the 6-DOF Modelica model to compiling it with CasADi and running MPC path following.
      This is the capstone of the tutorial series, tying together everything from the previous sections.
    </p>
    <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed mt-3">
      The aircraft model is being ported from the
      <a href="https://github.com/CogniPilot/cubs2" class="text-teal hover:text-accent transition-colors">CogniPilot CUBS2</a>
      project into Modelica, replacing hand-written CasADi code with generated code from Rumoca.
    </p>
  </div>
</TutorialLayout>
